From b3a5dbeebb7eb5dfc6796481367d5a6584624ede Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:17:11 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH bpf-next 7/8] sctp: expose referenced association socket
 lookup to XDP

An XDP receive policy can use TCP/UDP lookup to read application hints
from socket storage, but SCTP associations have no equivalent interface.
Expose an advisory association lookup in the ingress device's network
namespace, constrained by the ingress interface and L3 master context.

Hold a transport reference while taking a socket reference. The transport
pins its association; RCU and the endpoint's socket reference protect the
socket acquisition during accept/peeloff. Return an acquired socket and
provide a matching release kfunc so the verifier enforces its lifetime.

Only existing associations match. This is neither SCTP packet validation
nor final demultiplexing, and it does not claim a snapshot remains current
after peeloff. CPU hints, tuple domains and selection policy stay in BPF.
Register with the SCTP module lifetime, unwind protocol registration on
errors and keep BPF_SYSCALL=n builds independent of BPF registration.

Assisted-by: LLM
