diff --git a/Documentation/bpf/sctp-lookup.rst b/Documentation/bpf/sctp-lookup.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..d4ebe47fc3ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/bpf/sctp-lookup.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+SCTP socket lookup from XDP
+==========================
+
+An XDP program can look up the socket of an existing SCTP association in
+the ingress device's network namespace. This allows an early receive policy
+to read socket local storage without maintaining a second association table.
+It does not require CONFIG_RPS or select a receive CPU in the SCTP stack.
+
+With CONFIG_IP_SCTP and CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL, SCTP registers::
+
+    extern struct sock *bpf_xdp_sctp_lookup(struct xdp_md *ctx,
+                                           struct bpf_sock_tuple *tuple,
+                                           __u32 tuple__sz) __ksym;
+    extern void bpf_sctp_release(struct sock *sk) __ksym;
+
+Use sizeof(tuple->ipv4) or sizeof(tuple->ipv6) for tuple__sz. Addresses and
+ports are in network byte order, with source identifying the peer and
+destination identifying the local endpoint. IPv6 needs CONFIG_IPV6. The
+ingress interface and its L3 master context constrain the transport lookup.
+The verifier checks the memory region; the implementation checks tuple size.
+
+Lookup returns NULL for an invalid tuple size or absent association. It
+does not return an ordinary listening endpoint. An association on a
+one-to-many socket may return that shared socket. Release every non-NULL
+result using bpf_sctp_release on every path; the verifier tracks this
+reference. XDP socket storage access can use the returned socket.
+
+The transport lookup holds an association reference while acquiring the
+socket reference. RCU protects acquisition against a concurrent accept or
+peeloff changing the association's socket. The acquired socket reference
+remains valid independently of association teardown. This is only a safe
+snapshot: the association may move, the socket may close, or another socket
+may ultimately consume the packet.
+
+Lookup precedes routing and final SCTP demultiplexing. It does not validate
+verification tags, checksums, chunks or the SCTP state machine. NAT, VRF and
+policy routing must be accounted for by the caller. Distinct tuples of a
+multihomed association do not form a shared ordering domain merely because
+they resolve to the same socket.
+
+These GPL-only kfuncs are not a stable userspace ABI. Modular SCTP must be
+loaded, with usable module BTF, before a program referencing its kfuncs is
+loaded. A policy can use weak declarations to supply a fallback when the
+kfuncs are unavailable.
+
+The xdp_sctp_lookup selftest covers IPv4/IPv6 socket storage, invalid tuple
+sizes, verifier reference tracking, and lookup concurrent with peeloff and
+socket close. Run it with SCTP and IPv6 configured.
